{"parents": [{"link": "../", "title": "Available Types"}], "prev": {"link": "../StoryAreaTypeMessage/", "title": "StoryAreaTypeMessage"}, "next": {"link": "../StoryAreaTypeUniqueGift/", "title": "StoryAreaTypeUniqueGift"}, "title": "StoryAreaTypeWeather", "meta": null, "body": "<section id=\"storyareatypeweather\">\n<h1>StoryAreaTypeWeather<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#storyareatypeweather\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1>\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyrogram.types.StoryAreaTypeWeather\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyrogram.types.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">StoryAreaTypeWeather</span></span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#pyrogram.types.StoryAreaTypeWeather\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>This object describes a story area containing weather information. Currently, a story can have up to 3 weather areas.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>temperature</strong> (<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></code>) \u2013 Temperature, in degree Celsius.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>emoji</strong> (<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></code>) \u2013 Emoji representing the weather.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>background_color</strong> (<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">int</span></code>) \u2013 A color of the area background in the ARGB format.</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</section>\n", "metatags": "<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n", "rellinks": [["genindex", "General Index", "I", "index"], ["py-modindex", "Python Module Index", "", "modules"], 